ot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Self-Healing Documentation Fixes\n\nThis PR was automatically created by the Daily Documentation Healer workflow.\n\n### Gaps Fixed\n\n- Issue #66656: `[deep-report] Name the unsupported CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN instead of silently failing auth` — the issue was closed as completed by PR #66669, which added an explicit `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is not supported for Claude workflows; use ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or configure Anthropic Workload Identity Federation instead` error to the `gh aw` CLI secret setup path (interactive add and `secrets bootstrap`). That PR only changed Go code (`pkg/cli/engine_secrets.go` and tests) — it did not touch documentation. The two docs call-out sites the issue itself named, `docs/src/content/docs/setup/quick-start.mdx:151` and `docs/src/content/docs/setup/cli.md:232`, still described the pre-fix behavior (\"silently ignored\", \"an authentication error from the Claude CLI that never mentions the token\"). Updated both to describe the current explicit, named error.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nDDUw's closed-issue heuristic (`daily-doc-updater.md`, Step 1c, \"closed as completed\" branch) treats the existence of any merged PR that closes an issue by number as proof the gap is resolved, without checking what that PR actually changed. Issue #66656 was explicitly about two documentation lines, but its closing PR (#66669) was a code-only fix, so DDUw's heuristic would skip the issue as \"already addressed\" even though the referenced doc text was left stale and now describes behavior that no longer matches the code.\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 DDUw Improvement Suggestions</summary>\n\n### DDUw Improvement Suggestions\n\nIn Step 1c's \"closed as completed\" branch, after finding a merged PR that references the issue (whether via a `[docs]` PR, a `closes/fixes/resolves #NNN` match, or the spec-librarian fallback), add a file-scope check before treating the gap as resolved:\n\n1. Call `pull_request_read` with `method: get_files` on the closing PR.\n2. If none of the changed paths fall under `docs/src/content/docs/**`, do not assume the documentation change is complete — instead apply the existing \"direct content check\" sub-step (parse the issue body for referenced file paths/line numbers, read those files, and verify the specific described gap is still present) before skipping.\n3. Only skip the issue once the direct content check confirms the referenced documentation already matches the new behavior.\n\nThis closes the gap where a code-only fix PR silently satisfies DDUw's \"already handled\" heuristic for an issue that was fundamentally about stale documentation.\n\n</details>\n\n### Related Issues\n\n- Closes #66656\n\n\n<!-- gh-aw-tracker-id: daily-doc-healer -->\n\n> Generated by [📝 Daily Documentation Healer](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/actions/runs/37861087906) · claude · sonnet50 · 289.6 AIC · ⌖ 34.2 AIC · ⊞ 6.6K · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agithub%2Fgh-aw+%22gh-aw-workflow-id%3A+daily-doc-healer%22&type=pullrequests)\n> - [x] expires <!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-10-11T23:57:31.596Z --> on Oct 11, 2026, 3:57 PM UTC-08:00\n\n<!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Daily Documentation Healer, gh-aw-tracker-id: daily-doc-healer, engine: claude, model: claude-sonnet-5, id: 37861087906, workflow_id: daily-doc-healer, run: https://github.com/github/gh-aw/actions/runs/37861087906 -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-expires-type: pull-request -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: daily-doc-healer -->\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: github/gh-aw/daily-doc-healer -->","labels":[{"id":9099894122,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPc1QR88AAAACHmVdag","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","description":"Improvements or additions to documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9139391526,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPc1QR88AAAACIMAMJg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/labels/automation","name":"automat